
Jutze Japan Motion Coordinate Board ver. 1 (PBJP1501A)

The following macros are available to control some BSP options during
compile time:

MCB_USE_SPI
  define to enable on-board SPI bus on SCI4.

MCB_USE_I2C
  define to enable on-board I2C bus on SCI2.

MCB_USE_DAC124S085
  define to enable the DAC124S085 device.

MCB_USE_RS485
  define to enable the RS485 ports on SCI6 and SCI7.

MCB_USE_PCA9698
  define to enable the on-board PCA9698 bus expanders.

MCB_USE_PCA9698_I2C_EXT
  define to enable the PCA9698 bus expanders on I2C expansion (CN5).

MCB_USE_PCD4641
  define to enable the PCD4641 device.

MCB_USE_MCX514
  define to enable the MCX514 device.

MCB_USE_MCX514_I2C_EXT
  define to enable the MCX514 device on I2C expansion (CN5).

MCB_USE_USB
  define to enable USB.

MCB_USE_TRIGGER_IO
  define to enable the board specific trigger_io device.

MCB_USE_LEDS
  define to enable the board specific led_outputs device.

MCB_USE_DIPSWITCH
  define to enable the board specific dipswitch_inputs device.

MCB_USE_DIGITAL_IO
  define to enable the board specific digital_io device.

MCB_USE_ETHERC
  define to enable the RX63N EtherC device.

MCB_USE_FCU
  define to enable the FCU.

MCB_USE_SCI_DEBUG
  define to redirect debugging printf on stdout and stderr to the
  SCI debugging port.

MCB_USE_SCI0_RS232C
  define to enable the RS232-C port on CN7 (SCI0).

MCB_NO_CRC
  define to disable the RX63N hardware CRC accelerator device usage.

MCB_NO_RESET_HW_INIT
  do not initialize hardware as it is needed for a hard reset/boot.
  this option can be used to avoid re-initializing the hardware when switching
  to programs in RAM.

MCB_NO_PERIPHERAL_RESET_RELEASE
  do not assert or release the peripheral reset line during and after
  board init.

RX_USER_BOOT_IMAGE
  has to be set when building an image for the user boot area.
  the user boot area contains a pointer to the board info structure, which
  has to be set when building the user boo area image, but not when building
  a normal image.

RX_TEXT_IN_RAM
  define this when the .text section will be loaded into RAM, i.e. it is known
  that the CPU will always execute from RAM.  this is used by the FCU driver
  to tweak the code.
